mber><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6326718-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6326718</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1037431A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations> </citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IITSUKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NANKOU TAKAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKATSUJI AYAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IITSUKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NANKOU, TAKAHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKATSUJI, AYAKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IITSUKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NANKOU TAKAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKATSUJI AYAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IITSUKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NANKOU, TAKAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKATSUJI, AYAKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bus system in which a node identifier is allocated to each node, wherein when data files are transmitted from a transmission node (1) to a reception node (2), a control node (3) issues to the node (1) a command including the identifier of the node (2) and the value of the field representing the number of data files to be transmitted to carry out the data transfer, the node (1) ends the data transfer by instructing, if the number of data files is one or more, the node (2) to end the transfer when the transmission of the data files the number of which is specified by the field is ended, and the node (1) continues the transmission of the data file if the value of the field is zero thereby to adopt automatic shut-off after the data transfer under the leadership of the data transmission node, whereby issuance of commands is limited to a requisite minimum, and efficient processing is achieved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un système de bus dans lequel un identificateur de noeuds est attribué à chaque noeud. Selon ce système, lorsque les fichiers de données sont transmis d'un noeud de transmission (1) à un noeud de réception (2), un noeud de commande (3) envoie au noeud (1) une commande comprenant l'identificateur du noeud (2) et la valeur du champ représentant le nombre de fichiers de données à transmettre pour effectuer le transfert de données. Le noeud (1) met fin au transfert de données en commandant, lorsque le nombre de fichiers de données est supérieur ou égal à 1, le noeud (2) pour mettre fin au transfert, une fois les fichiers de données, dont le nombre est spécifié par le champ, transférés. Le noeud (1) poursuit la transmission des fichiers de données si la valeur du champ est égale à zéro, pour assurer ainsi un arrêt automatique une fois les données transférées sous la direction du noeud de transmission de données. Ce système permet de limiter l'émission de commandes au minimum nécessaire, et d'assurer un traitement efficace.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>